RISC-V: normalize a small-typed parameter once in the prolog instead of at every load (applies after
perf-43 and perf-74).

A bool/byte/short parameter is normalize-on-load: a caller may pass an unnarrowed int (IL allows the
implicit truncation, and the JIT's callers do not narrow), so morph wraps every load of it in a cast,
and a method that tests a bool parameter in a loop re-does andi 0xff each time. A small-typed
parameter in one register that is never stored to or address-exposed (lvNormalizedSmallParam, found
with the other extension facts in ComputeSignExtendedLocals) is now normalized once at the end of
genHomeRegisterParams, in the register it starts the method in, when it is live there; its loads drop
the cast (RemoveRedundantExtensions); a load from its stack home (not enregistered) uses the narrow
lbu/lb/lhu/lh instead of lw, and a reload after a spill already did. The extension predicates know
the value is extended.

Nethermind stateless guest on ZisK (most of it a bool tested per lane in KeccakHash.AbsorbLanes):
steps -37,097 / -68,645 (-0.07% / -0.05%) and cost -2.52M / -4.67M on blocks 26055159 / 26112793.
Outputs identical on 11 mainnet blocks.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/codegencommon.cpp
@@ -3745,6 +3745,37 @@
             GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R(INS_sext_w, EA_4BYTE, incomingReg, incomingReg);
         }
     }
+
+    // A small-typed parameter holds whatever its caller passed; one that is never redefined is normalized here,
+    // in the register it starts the method in, instead of at every load (see Lowering::ComputeSignExtendedLocals).
+    for (unsigned lclNum = 0; lclNum < m_compiler->info.compArgsCount; lclNum++)
+    {
+        const LclVarDsc* const varDsc = m_compiler->lvaGetDesc(lclNum);
+        if (!varDsc->lvNormalizedSmallParam || !varDsc->lvIsInReg() || !varDsc->lvTracked ||
+            !VarSetOps::IsMember(m_compiler, m_compiler->fgFirstBB->bbLiveIn, varDsc->lvVarIndex))
+        {
+            continue;
+        }
+
+        const regNumber reg        = varDsc->GetRegNum();
+        const unsigned  size       = genTypeSize(varDsc->TypeGet());
+        const bool      isUnsigned = varTypeIsUnsigned(varDsc->TypeGet());
+        if ((size == 1) && isUnsigned)
+        {
+            GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_I(INS_andi, EA_PTRSIZE, reg, reg, 0xff);
+        }
+        else if (m_compiler->compOpportunisticallyDependsOn(InstructionSet_Zbb))
+        {
+            GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R((size == 1) ? INS_sext_b : (isUnsigned ? INS_zext_h : INS_sext_h), EA_PTRSIZE,
+                                      reg, reg);
+        }
+        else
+        {
+            const unsigned shift = 64 - size * 8;
+            GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_I(INS_slli, EA_PTRSIZE, reg, reg, shift);
+            GetEmitter()->emitIns_R_R_I(isUnsigned ? INS_srli : INS_srai, EA_PTRSIZE, reg, reg, shift);
+        }
+    }
 #endif // TARGET_RISCV64
 }
 
